From: Raphael Herouart <rherouart@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:38:28 +0100
Subject: [M156] [runtime] Check prototypes and exceptions in
 SetPrototypeProperties

Original change's description:
> [runtime] Check prototypes and exceptions in SetPrototypeProperties
>
> `IsDefaultFunctionPrototype` accepted dictionary-mode `JSTypedArray` and
> `JSPrimitiveWrapper` objects. `Runtime_SetPrototypeProperties` then took
> the fast path on exotic receivers and bypassed `JSTypedArray` index
> invariants.
>
> `Runtime_SetPrototypeProperties` also called `.Check()` on fallible
> property writes. When `SetDataProperty`, `TransitionAndWriteDataProperty`,
> or `SetAccessor` threw an exception, V8 crashed in `v8::FromJust`.
>
> This CL makes three changes:
> - Check that default function prototypes have `JS_OBJECT_TYPE` and empty
>   elements.
> - Use `SetPrototypePropertiesSlow` for functions without a prototype
>   property and for exotic, shared, intercepted, or access-checked
>   prototypes.
> - Propagate exceptions from `SetDataProperty`,
>   `TransitionAndWriteDataProperty`, and `SetAccessor`.
>
> Fixed: 578083257, 577944790
